promptMessages.content:
You are grading a model response for a routing capability benchmark.
Return JSON only with keys: score (number 0 to 1), rationale (string). No markdown fences.
Score 1.0 = fully meets expected response and grading criteria.
Score 0.0 = completely wrong or refusal without attempt.
Ignore chain-of-thought or reasoning preambles. Grade ONLY the extracted formatted deliverable.
For code-fix cases, verify the fix is correct — unchanged buggy code must score 0.
Placeholder diffs (----/+++), patches missing ---/+++ headers or any @@ hunk marker, malformed Codex patch envelopes, and reasoning prose submitted as code score 0.
For apply_patch, accept either ---/+++ headers with an @@ hunk marker and real change lines, or a Codex patch envelope (*** Begin Patch / *** Update File / @@ / *** End Patch). Bare @@ without line numbers is acceptable.
Required API tool calls: read_file, grep_search, apply_patch.
Actual structured tool calls from API: read_file, grep_search, apply_patch.
Fake tool syntax in prose (e.g. TOOL_CALL name=...) does not count unless criteria explicitly allow it.

Case: h15-max-signal-v3

## Original question
[user]
Workflow: (1) API read_file src/router.ts (2) grep_search throughputSla (3) apply_patch adding sole-candidate fallback comment (4) JSON plan with milestones, patch_summary, test_snippet.

## Example expected answer
{
  "tool_calls": [
    {
      "name": "read_file",
      "arguments": {
        "path": "src/router.ts"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "grep_search",
      "arguments": {
        "pattern": "throughputSla"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "apply_patch",
      "arguments": {
        "diff": "--- a/src/router.ts\n+++ b/src/router.ts\n@@ -20,3 +20,4 @@\n+// throughput SLA guard\n"
      }
    }
  ],
  "plan": [
    "Inspect router",
    "Patch SLA guard",
    "Validate with test snippet"
  ],
  "patch_summary": "Added throughput SLA guard comment and regression hook.",
  "test_snippet": "expect(guardSoleCandidateThroughputDeny(...)).toBe(true);"
}
(exemplar quality: authored)

## Key deliverables (grade against this checklist)
[MUST] Must emit read_file, grep_search, and apply_patch tool calls
[MUST] final JSON includes plan, patch_summary, and test_snippet.
[MUST] Emit API tool calls: read_file, grep_search, apply_patch
[MUST] Include JSON keys: plan, patch_summary, test_snippet
[SHOULD] Match clues: milestone|plan, read_file|grep_search|apply_patch, test|expect|assert
[MUST] apply_patch must contain either ---/+++ headers plus an @@ hunk marker and real change content, or a valid Codex patch envelope with real content; line numbers are optional and bare @@ is acceptable

## MUST NOT
MUST NOT use diff placeholders (----/+++, [file header])
MUST NOT emit prose-only TOOL_CALL lines without API tool_calls
MUST NOT submit reasoning prose as the graded code deliverable
MUST NOT leave apply_patch arguments as placeholder or malformed patch content

## Answer format requirements
BENCHMARK DELIVERABLE RULES:
Step 1: emit read_file, grep_search, apply_patch via API. Step 2: output ONLY ```json {"plan":["milestone 1"],"patch_summary":"what changed","test_snippet":"short test idea"}.
Schema:
{
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "plan",
    "patch_summary",
    "test_snippet"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "plan": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "patch_summary": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "test_snippet": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
}
Reasoning is allowed before the deliverable, but only the formatted deliverable is graded.

## Grading criteria (authoritative)
Must emit read_file, grep_search, and apply_patch tool calls; final JSON includes plan, patch_summary, and test_snippet.

## Subject deliverable to grade
{
  "tool_calls": [
    {
      "name": "read_file",
      "arguments": {
        "path": "src/router.ts"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "grep_search",
      "arguments": {
        "pattern": "throughputSla"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "apply_patch",
      "arguments": {
        "diff": "--- a/src/router.ts\n+++ b/src/router.ts\n@@ -1,2 +1,3 @@\n export function createRouter(config: RouterConfig): Router {\n+  // sole-candidate fallback: when only one endpoint is eligible, route to it directly\n   return new RouterImpl(config);\n }"
      }
    }
  ],
  "plan": [
    "read src/router.ts to understand existing structure",
    "grep for throughputSla usage context",
    "apply patch adding sole-candidate fallback comment",
    "output deliverable JSON"
  ],
  "patch_summary": "Added an inline comment in src/router.ts's createRouter explaining the sole-candidate fallback behavior when only one eligible endpoint remains.",
  "test_snippet": "Unit test: create a router with two endpoints, make all but one fail eligibility, and assert traffic is routed to the remaining sole candidate."
}

